  "releaseNotes": "## 12.3.1\n\n### Security\n- SixLabors.ImageSharp goes from 4.0.0 to 4.1.2, which fixes GHSA-jjfr-hcj7-qf5w, GHSA-ffp7-56pq-64mr, GHSA-j9gm-c75j-xc9q, GHSA-j3p4-wp97-rph4, GHSA-4q3p-rj5x-xv7p, GHSA-wmxv-xphr-5c9g and GHSA-gwg2-r3hj-4w44 (out-of-bounds writes in the TIFF CCITT encoders and ICC LUT16 handling, unchecked allocation in ICC CLUT parsing, stale data from the EXR ZIP decoder, a BigTIFF decode loop that never progresses, and an unchecked index in histogram equalization). Nothing else changes.",
